{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01L1c6tV8DM8xuotE3SgXRNC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#pragma once\n2\t\n3\t#include <stdio.h>\n4\t\n5\t#include \"token.h\"\n6\t\n7\t// The maximum number of tokens we can put back.\n8\t#define TOKEN_PUTBACKS 5\n9\t\n10\t// This is a lexer structure, which will contain all of the information about\n11\t// the state of a lexer.\n12\ttypedef struct {\n13\t    FILE *fp; // The file we are reading from.\n14\t    char current_file[TOKEN_LENGTH]; // The name of source file we are reading from.\n15\t    char buffer[1]; // A buffer so that chars can be \"put back\"\n16\t    long position; // The posistion of the file pointer in the current file in characters from the start\n17\t    int last_column;\n18\t    int column; // The number of characters down whichever line its on\n19\t    int line; // The number of lines it has passed so far\n20\t    Token unlexed[TOKEN_PUTBACKS];\n21\t    unsigned unlexed_count;\n22\t} Lexer;\n23\t\n24\t// Takes an open file pointer, and a token as input. It fills the token struct\n25\t// with the next available token from the file.\n26\tint lex(Lexer *l, Token *token);\n27\t\n28\t// Wrapper for getc. Takes a lexer pointer and returns the next character in the file its holding onto.\n29\t// Updates position and stream\n30\tint lexer_getchar(Lexer *l);\n31\t\n32\t// Wrapper for ungetc. Takes a lexer pointer and back-tracks 1 character using the lexer buffer. Updates position\n33\tint lexer_ungetchar(Lexer *l);\n34\t\n35\t// Put a token back to be lexed again in the future.\n36\tint unlex(Lexer *l, Token *token);\n37\t\n38\t// Find token type for single char\n39\tTokenType ttype_one_char(char c);\n40\t\n41\t// Find token type for a char* with multiple characters\n42\tTokenType ttype_many_chars(const char *contents);\n43\t\n44\t// Discern the token type from the given contents of unknown length\n45\tTokenType ttype_from_string(const char *contents);\n46\t\n47\t// Jump to next token by skipping whitespace and comments (doesn't read it)\n48\tint skip_to_token(Lexer *l);\n49\t\n50\t// Get the string representation of a token type.\n51\t// E.g. TT_EOF -> \"end of file\", TT_LITERAL -> \"literal\", etc.\n52\tconst char *ttype_name(TokenType tt);\n53\t\n54\t// Test for ttype_from_string\n55\tint test_ttype_from_string();\n56\t\n57\tint test_ttype_many_chars();\n58\t\n59\tint test_ttype_one_char();\n60\t\n61\tint test_ttype_name();\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7a3d076-6fed-463e-a78f-078e79794145","uuid":"46f84758-319b-467d-a7ba-05add504b9c2","timestamp":"2026-06-06T06:17:42.060Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-crust-fwVZds/project/c_src/src/lexer/lex.h","content":"#pragma once\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n\n#include \"token.h\"\n\n// The maximum number of tokens we can put back.\n#define TOKEN_PUTBACKS 5\n\n// This is a lexer structure, which will contain all of the information about\n// the state of a lexer.\ntypedef struct {\n    FILE *fp; // The file we are reading from.\n    char current_file[TOKEN_LENGTH]; // The name of source file we are reading from.\n    char buffer[1]; // A buffer so that chars can be \"put back\"\n    long position; // The posistion of the file pointer in the current file in characters from the start\n    int last_column;\n    int column; // The number of characters down whichever line its on\n    int line; // The number of lines it has passed so far\n    Token unlexed[TOKEN_PUTBACKS];\n    unsigned unlexed_count;\n} Lexer;\n\n// Takes an open file pointer, and a token as input. It fills the token struct\n// with the next available token from the file.\nint lex(Lexer *l, Token *token);\n\n// Wrapper for getc. Takes a lexer pointer and returns the next character in the file its holding onto.\n// Updates position and stream\nint lexer_getchar(Lexer *l);\n\n// Wrapper for ungetc. Takes a lexer pointer and back-tracks 1 character using the lexer buffer. Updates position\nint lexer_ungetchar(Lexer *l);\n\n// Put a token back to be lexed again in the future.\nint unlex(Lexer *l, Token *token);\n\n// Find token type for single char\nTokenType ttype_one_char(char c);\n\n// Find token type for a char* with multiple characters\nTokenType ttype_many_chars(const char *contents);\n\n// Discern the token type from the given contents of unknown length\nTokenType ttype_from_string(const char *contents);\n\n// Jump to next token by skipping whitespace and comments (doesn't read it)\nint skip_to_token(Lexer *l);\n\n// Get the string representation of a token type.\n// E.g. TT_EOF -> \"end of file\", TT_LITERAL -> \"literal\", etc.\nconst char *ttype_name(TokenType tt);\n\n// Test for ttype_from_string\nint test_ttype_from_string();\n\nint test_ttype_many_chars();\n\nint test_ttype_one_char();\n\nint test_ttype_name();\n","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62}}}
